# SITE 00 uppercase brand typography (mandatory)

Applies to **all SITE 00 surfaces** (`src/site00/**`, routes under `/origin`, `/sites`, `/services`, `/enter`, `/assts`, `/control`, `/idnty`, `/bldr`, etc.).

## Rule

**ALL visible text must be UPPERCASE.**

**Only exception:** password `<input>` fields (including when toggled to visible text via show/hide — keep `.site00-signin-form__input--password`).

## Overrides design references

When implementing pages from reference images, storyboards, or Figma exports:

- **Do not** preserve sentence case or title case from the reference.
- **Always** convert user-visible copy to uppercase in source strings **and** rely on the global CSS safety net in `site00-typography.css` (`.site00-shell`, `.site00-public-shell`, `.site00-ctrl-room-shell`, `.site00-mobile-shell`, `.site00-assts-shell`, etc.).

## Implementation checklist

1. Seed/config copy (`site00-page-seed.ts`, `directory.ts`, `builder.ts`, `identity.ts`, page TSX) — uppercase literals.
2. Search placeholders — uppercase (e.g. `SEARCH TEMPLATES…`).
3. Never add `text-transform: none` on SITE 00 text except password inputs.
4. Email addresses, URLs in copy, and dynamic user email display — uppercase is correct for SITE 00 brand.

## Do not

- Lowercase labels, body copy, empty states, or nav items to match a reference mock.
- Use Frontal Slayer typography rules inside SITE 00.

